**Bonus thought — the "policy stack" view**

If you want a flagship demo for a firm-wide audience, the most impressive single move is to upload your entire policy stack to a SharePoint site, point Copilot Chat at it, and demo it as a **personal compliance assistant**: "Can I accept this invitation?" "Do I need to pre-clear this trade?" "Can I post this on LinkedIn?" "My spouse is interviewing at a public company — what do I do?" The same source documents power #1 through #9 above; this is the human-facing top layer.

One framing note for your audience: across all of these, the source PDF stays the authoritative document and Copilot output is always a derivative aid — FAQ, summary, training, flowchart — never the policy itself. That's the line legal and compliance will care about, and it's what makes these production-safe versus experimental.

Want me to pick one policy type (say Code of Ethics or Social Media) and build out the full workflow — FAQ, role guides, flowchart, training deck, quiz — as a single end-to-end demo arc? It's a powerful showcase because the audience sees one source document become five usable artifacts in front of them.
